{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>The sons of Aharon, the priests.</b> When they are in their priesthood — but an ordinary priest who served in the eight garments, his service is invalid (Zevachim 18)." "<b>The pieces, the head.</b> Because the head is not included in the flaying, since it was already severed at slaughter, therefore Scripture needed to count it separately (Chullin 27)." "<b>And the peder.</b> Why is this stated? To teach you that he places it with the head and covers the place of slaughter with it — and this is a mark of respect from above (ibid.)." "<b>That are on the altar.</b> That the logs should not extend outside the arrangement (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:35.573767978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}